This is a known breaking change. Android 15+ (and .NET MAUI 10 by default) enforces **edge-to-edge** rendering, which makes `adjustResize` ineffective. The replacement is **WindowInsets**-based handling.

### Quick fix — two options:

**Option 1: Opt in to automatic keyboard inset handling (recommended)**

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Compatibility.Platform.Android;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    // Let the framework automatically adjust for the IME (keyboard)
    WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);
    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new ImeInsetsListener());
}

private class ImeInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBar = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        v.SetPadding(
            systemBar.Left, systemBar.Top, systemBar.Right,
            Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBar.Bottom));

        return WindowInsetsCompat.Consumed;
    }
}
```

**Option 2: Simplest one-liner (if you just need `adjustPan` behavior)**

In `AndroidManifest.xml` on your `<activity>`:

```xml
android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustPan"
```

`adjustPan` was **not** deprecated and still scrolls the view so the focused input stays visible. It's less smooth than Option 1 but requires zero code.

### Why `Resize` stopped working

| .NET 9 | .NET 10 |
|---|---|
| `adjustResize` via `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | Android 15 deprecated `adjustResize` under edge-to-edge |
| System auto-shrinks the window | App must react to `WindowInsets.Type.Ime()` itself |

**Option 1** is the forward-looking solution — it gives you smooth animated resizing and works correctly with edge-to-edge. **Option 2** is a quick drop-in if you just need it working now.
